cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, cite the accompanying OTTP paper and this archived software version."
title: "OTTP: A Benchmark Protocol for Trajectory-Prefix Risk Prediction in Offline Safe Reinforcement Learning"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chai
    given-names: Yi
    affiliation: Shanghai University of Electric Power
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Dandan
    affiliation: Shanghai University of Electric Power
  - family-names: Luo
    given-names: Zixiao
    affiliation: Shanghai University of Electric Power
abstract: >-
  OTTP provides a reproducible protocol and benchmark for hindsight-defined
  trajectory-prefix cumulative-cost prediction on offline safe-RL logs. The
  primary endpoint is Step catastrophic AUPRC. The archive contains code,
  result tables, run records, and split and preprocessing artifacts.
keywords:
  - offline safe reinforcement learning
  - benchmark protocol
  - trajectory-prefix prediction
  - hindsight cumulative cost
license: MIT
version: "1.1.0"
